From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:24:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 116/118] scripting: in a 3D scene input.cursorWorldPosition is
 the cursor cast to the far plane

scenescript64's getter calls the host's vtable +0xa8 with flag 0: wallpaper64 GH 0x1401bcb00,
which unprojects (x, 1 - y, 0.5) through the frame's view (ctx +0x38) and projection (ctx +0x40)
with viewport (0, 0, 1, 1), glm style (NDC z = 2 * 0.5 - 1 = 0), and zeroes z when context flag
0x400 is set. WE's 3D projection is the renderer's vtable +0x10, GH 0x14009afd0: DirectXMath's
XMMatrixPerspectiveFovRH called with nearz and farz swapped (a reversed depth), where NDC z 0 is
the far plane. So the cursor's world position is the point on its ray at the view depth farz.
In an orthographic scene the same unprojection is scene pixels (x right, y up), as before.

3477054430's head turns toward cursorWorldPosition - its origin: in WE it turns left with the
pointer at the centre or the left (the far point is thousands of units left) and right at the
right; ours gave scene pixels and the head never turned that way. 3509243656 divides it by 8000 /
9000 (its farz is 10000). Ours unprojects with the camera's own world view-projection (GL clip,
far at z +1, y flipped) in double precision.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md (3477054430: we-ref captures ptrL-3d, ptrR-3d); docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "3D scenes against WE"
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
---
 .../WallpaperEngine/Scripting/InputObject.cpp  | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/InputObject.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/InputObject.cpp
index 0986963..05a794c 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/InputObject.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/InputObject.cpp
@@ -2,17 +2,33 @@
 
 #include "EngineObject.h"
 #include "ScriptEngine.h"
+#include "WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h"
 #include "WallpaperEngine/Render/Wallpapers/CScene.h"
 
+#include <glm/glm.hpp>
+
 using namespace WallpaperEngine::Scripting;
 
 JSValue get_cursor_world_position (JSContext* ctx, JSValueConst this_val, int argc, JSValueConst* argv) {
     JSClassID classId;
     auto* input = static_cast<InputObject*> (JS_GetAnyOpaque (this_val, &classId));
 
-    // the cursor in WE's world: scene pixels, x right, y up
+    // WE (wallpaper64 GH 0x1401bcb00, the script host's vtable +0xa8 that scenescript64's getter calls with flag 0):
+    // glm-style unProject of (x, 1 − y, 0.5) through the frame's view and projection, viewport (0, 0, 1, 1), so NDC z 0.
+    // Its 3D projection is DirectXMath's PerspectiveFovRH with nearz and farz swapped (GH 0x14009afd0: a reversed
+    // depth), where NDC z 0 is the far plane: in a 3D scene the cursor is the point on its ray at the view depth farz
+    // (3477054430's head turns toward it, 3509243656 divides it by 8000 / 9000 at farz 10000). An orthographic
+    // scene's unProject is scene pixels, x right, y up, z 0 (ctx flag 0x400 zeroes z).
     const auto& scene = input->getScene ();
     const glm::vec2 position = *scene.getMousePositionNormalized ();
+    const auto& camera = scene.getCamera ();
+    if (camera.isPerspective ()) {
+	// ours: GL clip space, far at z +1, clip y flipped (the scene FBO is read top-down)
+	const glm::dmat4 inverse = glm::inverse (glm::dmat4 (camera.getWorldViewProjection ()));
+	const glm::dvec4 world = inverse
+	    * glm::dvec4 (2.0 * position.x - 1.0, 2.0 * position.y - 1.0, 1.0, 1.0);
+	return scene.getScriptEngine ().newVec (glm::vec3 (glm::dvec3 (world) / world.w));
+    }
     return scene.getScriptEngine ().newVec (glm::vec3 (
 	position.x * static_cast<float> (scene.getWidth ()), (1.0f - position.y) * static_cast<float> (scene.getHeight ()),
 	0.0f
